//
// A DECODED VIEW ANSWERS WHAT ITS COPY WOULD, ACROSS EVERY RULE IT MEETS (`@FR-R-DecodeView`).  A
// decoded record's `text` or `vector<u8>` field may hold a span of the frame's bytes instead of a
// copy; wherever it meets another rule — a byte copy out of the frame, a text run, a value that
// escapes the frame, a callee that reads in place — every read answers what the owned copy would.
// Each section is one crossing, with its own cases and receipt.
//
// ── a-byte-string-copied-out-of-a-frame-is-the-frames-bytes-at-the-decode ──
//
// A BYTE STRING COPIED OUT OF A FRAME IS THE FRAME'S BYTES AT THE DECODE (`@FR-R-DecodeView` crossed
// with `@FR-R-ByteCopy`).  R-DecodeView lets a `vector<u8>` field whose value at construction is "a
// span B[a..b] of a byte vector B — … copied by (R-ByteCopy)'s vector clause" hold the SPAN instead
// of an owned copy, when the frame B is not written until the field's last read and the field is
// read only as a value; otherwise the field stays owned.  R-ByteCopy is the decoder's
// `for k in 0..arg { bs += [bytes[at + k] ?? 0] }`, one slice append behind its guard.  Every road
// answers the bytes the frame held at the decode: decoded byte strings never read (the span road on
// `--native-release`), read as a length, an equality with a literal and a fold (the owned road),
// read after the frame is written, and copied into an owned slot before the frame is written.
//
// The decoder is loft's `tests/scripts/a-decoded-text-is-read-where-it-lies.loft` `read_v` (tag 1 an
// integer, 2 a text, 3 a byte string, 4 a map; a length byte, then the bytes).
//
// Values hand-computed over frame3() = { "op": "apply", "raw": b"hi", "k": b"xyz" }:
//   count_entries → 3 (two byte strings decoded, none read)
//   bytes_eq("raw") → 2 / [104,105] equal / fold 104·7 + 105 = 833 → "2/true/833"
//   bytes_eq("k")   → 3 / false / ((120·7 + 121)·7 + 122) = 6849 → "3/false/6849"
//   bytes_scribble("k"): the frame's last byte set to 33 after the decode → "3/120/122"
//   bytes_copied("k"): own = the byte string, then the frame's last byte set to 34 → "3/122"
//   a truncated frame (the byte string's length past the end) → "?" (no value decoded)
//
// Axes it MOVES: the byte string's use (none, length, equality, fold, element reads, a copy into an
//   owned slot), the frame written after the decode or not, a well-formed and a truncated frame.
//
// Cross-backend; `main` runs every cell so the leak gate reads the file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; every cell answered as hand-computed, interpret,
//   native and (by hand) --native-release, and the same under LOFT_NO_DECODE_VIEW=1 and
//   LOFT_NO_BYTE_COPY=1.  Fires on --native-release only (the suite's lanes do not reach it):
//   LOFT_TRACE_DECODE_VIEW=1 says `n_count_entries: a root over `frame``; `n_bytes_eq` and
//   `n_bytes_copied` decline "a read of a decoded byte string", `n_bytes_scribble` "an element
//   address of the frame outside a read" — today every byte-string READ keeps the field owned,
//   narrower than the rule's (4); the span road is reached by the unread byte strings only.
// CHANNEL: the asserts.
// ARMED: no instrument (the switches above, by hand).
// WITNESS: each message prints the bytes read.
// HOLDS: loft `tests/scripts/a-decoded-text-is-read-where-it-lies.loft` (the text fields).
//
// ── a-decoded-text-span-reads-what-the-copy-would-at-every-byte-run ──
//
// A DECODED TEXT SPAN READS WHAT THE COPY WOULD, AT EVERY BYTE RUN (`@FR-R-DecodeView` crossed
// with `@FR-R-TextRun`).  R-DecodeView holds a decoded record's `text` field as a SPAN of the
// frame B when the field's value at construction "is a span B[a..b] of a byte vector B — read
// by (R-TextRun), copied by (R-ByteCopy)'s vector clause, or a slice", and condition (5): "the
// span's bytes ARE the text the owned form holds: text_from_bytes leaves them unchanged (valid
// UTF-8, tested once at construction).  A span that would be converted builds the owned text".
// R-TextRun turns `t: vector<u8> = []; for i in lo..hi { t += [v[off + i] ?? d] }; x =
// text_from_bytes(t)` into a range read guarded by the copy's guard.  So the decoder's text
// leaf is a text run of the frame, and the span must answer, byte for byte, the text the
// built copy answers — for valid ASCII, valid multi-byte UTF-8, a run that is not UTF-8 (the
// copy answers ""), an empty run, a run ending exactly at the frame's end, and one that would
// run past it (the decode fails).
//
// The frame: a tag byte, 2 a text of the next `arg` bytes, 4 a map of `arg` key / value pairs,
// 1 an integer (arg - 100).  Values hand-computed in each cell's comment.
//
// Firing read under `LOFT_TRACE_DECODE_VIEW=1` on `loft --native-release <cell>` (`main`): the
// roots `shout`, `measure` and `lookup` admitted.  The view clause is planned only for a build
// without the live tier — `--native-release` — so plain `--native` and the suite's `--tests`
// lanes keep every field owned and check the values only; `LOFT_NO_DECODE_VIEW=1` and
// `LOFT_NO_BYTE_COPY=1` (no text run, hence no span) answer the same.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the rule's own receipt (a span one byte late)
//   answers d1's lookups `-`.
// CHANNEL: the asserts, on --native-release.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: each message prints the decoded text.
// HOLDS: the interpreter keeps every field owned and is the oracle.
//
// ── a-decoded-value-that-escapes-its-frame-is-built-owned ──
//
// A DECODED VALUE THAT ESCAPES ITS FRAME IS BUILT OWNED (`@FR-R-DecodeView` crossed with
// `@FR-R-Escape`).  R-DecodeView holds decoded text fields as spans of the frame B only where
// R holds no further than frames B outlives: "(2) R is CONFINED to frames that hold B ... A
// return hands R to a caller only where that call passed B ... and the condition is decided
// over EVERY call site in the unit (R-Escape); one site that cannot be shown confined declines
// the function", "(3) no holder lets R cross a boundary: a return out of the frame that owns
// B, a store into a collection or field that outlives B, ... a closure capture".  R-Escape is
// the licence and its limit: a construction that ESCAPES keeps the representation the program
// promised.  So each cell decodes a frame and lets the value — or a part of it — out by one
// road, then rewrites or drops the frame, and reads the escaped value: it must be the text the
// frame held at the decode, never what the frame's bytes are now.
//
// Axes it MOVES: the road out (a text copied into an owned slot — admitted, the value
// returned from the root, an entry appended to a caller's collection, the frame written after
// the decode, a capture), what happens to the frame after (rewritten, its owner returns).
// The frame: tag 2 a text of `arg` bytes, 4 a map of `arg` pairs, 1 an integer.  Values
// hand-computed in each cell's comment.
//
// Firing read under `LOFT_TRACE_DECODE_VIEW=1` on `loft --native-release <cell>` (`main`): `held`
// a root; `keep` declined ("a decoded value returned out of its frame"), `scribble` declined
// ("an element address of the frame outside a read"); `stash` never a candidate (its second
// parameter is a collection) and e5's frame a local, which instance 1 does not admit.  The
// view clause is planned only without the live tier, so the suite's lanes check the values;
// `LOFT_NO_DECODE_VIEW=1` answers the same.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; a span kept for a returned value would read the
//   rewritten frame in e2 (`zzzz` for `ping`).
// CHANNEL: the asserts, on --native-release.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: each message prints the text read.
// HOLDS: the interpreter is the oracle.
//
// ── an-in-place-callee-reads-a-decoded-text-where-it-lies ──
//
// AN IN-PLACE CALLEE READS A DECODED TEXT WHERE IT LIES (`@FR-R-DecodeView` crossed with
// `@FR-R-Callee`).  R-DecodeView emits "every function of the confined region that touches T … as a
// twin over that layout — the way (R-Callee) emits a twin over its inputs", so a decoded text field
// is read as a span of the frame by every helper the root hands it to.  R-Callee admits a callee
// whose store writes are all in-place scalar sets under the caller's loop hoist.  The two meet in
// `tally`: a helper in the decode region that READS a decoded text (its length, an equality) and
// WRITES only scalar fields of an accumulator in place, called per entry inside a loop that also
// reads the accumulator the callee writes.  Every count must be the owned road's: the bytes of each
// text, the equality against "op", and the accumulator's running fields after every call.
//
// The decoder is loft's `tests/scripts/a-decoded-text-is-read-where-it-lies.loft` `read_v`.
//
// Values hand-computed over frame3() = { "op": "apply", "raw": b"hi", "k": b"xyz" }:
//   tally_all: texts op(2) apply(5) raw(3) k(1) → n 4, bytes 11, hits 1 → "4 11 1"
//   tally_loop(3): keys only, per round n += 3, bytes += 6, hits += 1 (op), then hits += n:
//     round 1 → 3 6 4; round 2 → 6 12 11; round 3 → 9 18 21 → "9 18 21"
//
// Axes it MOVES: the callee's reads (a text's size, an equality), its writes (three scalar fields
//   in place), the caller (a single pass, a loop that also reads what the callee writes).
//
// Cross-backend; `main` runs every cell so the leak gate reads the file.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; every cell answered as hand-computed, interpret,
//   native and (by hand) --native-release, and the same under LOFT_NO_DECODE_VIEW=1.  Fires on
//   --native-release only: LOFT_TRACE_DECODE_VIEW=1 says `n_tally_all: a root over `frame`, region
//   4` and the same for `n_tally_loop`; LOFT_REWRITE_CENSUS_FN counts R-Callee in `n_tally_loop`.
// CHANNEL: the asserts.
// ARMED: no instrument (the switch above, by hand).
// WITNESS: each message prints the accumulator.
// HOLDS: `a-byte-string-copied-out-of-a-frame-is-the-frames-bytes-at-the-decode` beside it.

enum Val {
  VNull,
  VInt { value: integer },
  VText { value: text },
  VBytes { value: vector<u8> },
  VMap { entries: vector<Entry> },
}

struct Entry {
  key: Val,
  value: Val,
}

struct Dec {
  value: Val,
  next: integer,
  ok: boolean,
}

fn read_v(bytes: vector<u8>, pos: integer, depth: integer) -> Dec {
  n = len(bytes);
  if pos + 1 >= n || depth > 8 { return Dec { value: VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
  tag = bytes[pos] ?? 0;
  arg = bytes[pos + 1] ?? 0;
  at = pos + 2;
  if tag == 1 { return Dec { value: VInt { value: arg - 100 }, next: at, ok: true }; }
  if tag == 3 {
    if at + arg > n { return Dec { value: VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    bs: vector<u8> = [];
    for k in 0..arg { bs += [bytes[at + k] ?? 0]; }
    return Dec { value: VBytes { value: bs }, next: at + arg, ok: true };
  }
  if tag == 2 {
    if at + arg > n { return Dec { value: VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    tb: vector<u8> = [];
    for k in 0..arg { tb += [bytes[at + k] ?? 0]; }
    return Dec { value: VText { value: text_from_bytes(tb) }, next: at + arg, ok: true };
  }
  if tag == 4 {
    entries: vector<Entry> = [];
    p = at;
    mok = true;
    for _ in 0..arg {
      if mok {
        kd = read_v(bytes, p, depth + 1);
        if kd.ok {
          vd = read_v(bytes, kd.next, depth + 1);
          if vd.ok {
            kv = kd.value;
            vv = vd.value;
            entries += [Entry { key: kv, value: vv }];
            p = vd.next;
          } else { mok = false; }
        } else { mok = false; }
      }
    }
    if !mok { return Dec { value: VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    return Dec { value: VMap { entries: entries }, next: p, ok: true };
  }
  return Dec { value: VNull, next: pos, ok: false };
}

fn dec(bytes: vector<u8>) -> Dec { read_v(bytes, 0, 0) }

/// The entry of map `m` under text key `key`, or null.
fn get(m: Val, key: text) -> Val {
  match m {
    VMap { entries } => {
      for e in entries {
        match e.key { VText { value } => { if value == key { return e.value; } }, _ => {} }
      }
    },
    _ => {}
  }
  return VNull;
}

fn tb(t: text) -> vector<u8> {
  b: vector<u8> = [];
  for i in 0..size(t) { b += [(t.byte_at(i) & 255) as u8]; }
  b
}

/// map of 3: "op" -> text "apply", "raw" -> bytes "hi", "k" -> bytes "xyz"
fn frame3() -> vector<u8> {
  f: vector<u8> = [4, 3];
  f += [2, 2];
  f += tb("op");
  f += [2, 5];
  f += tb("apply");
  f += [2, 3];
  f += tb("raw");
  f += [3, 2];
  f += tb("hi");
  f += [2, 1];
  f += tb("k");
  f += [3, 3];
  f += tb("xyz");
  f
}

fn count_entries(frame: vector<u8>) -> integer {
  d = dec(frame);
  match d.value { VMap { entries } => { return len(entries); }, _ => {} }
  return -1;
}

fn bytes_eq(frame: vector<u8>, key: text) -> text {
  d = dec(frame);
  match get(d.value, key) {
    VBytes { value } => {
      s = 0;
      for b in value { s = s * 7 + b; }
      return "{len(value)}/{value == [104, 105]}/{s}";
    },
    _ => {}
  }
  return "?";
}

fn bytes_scribble(frame: vector<u8>, key: text) -> text {
  d = dec(frame);
  frame[len(frame) - 1] = 33;
  match get(d.value, key) {
    VBytes { value } => { return "{len(value)}/{value[0] ?? -1}/{value[len(value) - 1] ?? -1}"; },
    _ => {}
  }
  return "?";
}

fn bytes_copied(frame: vector<u8>, key: text) -> text {
  d = dec(frame);
  own: vector<u8> = [];
  match get(d.value, key) { VBytes { value } => { own = value; }, _ => {} }
  frame[len(frame) - 1] = 34;
  "{len(own)}/{own[len(own) - 1] ?? -1}"
}

fn test_unread_byte_strings_are_counted() {
  n = count_entries(frame3());
  assert(n == 3, "count: {n}");
}

fn test_a_read_byte_string_is_the_frames_bytes() {
  f = frame3();
  a = bytes_eq(f, "raw");
  b = bytes_eq(f, "k");
  assert(a == "2/true/833" && b == "3/false/6849", "reads: {a} {b}");
}

fn test_a_later_write_to_the_frame_is_not_seen() {
  g = frame3();
  h = frame3();
  a = bytes_scribble(g, "k");
  b = bytes_copied(h, "k");
  assert(a == "3/120/122" && b == "3/122", "after a write: {a} {b}");
}

fn test_a_truncated_byte_string_decodes_nothing() {
  t: vector<u8> = [3, 9, 1, 2];
  a = bytes_eq(t, "raw");
  assert(a == "?", "truncated: {a}");
}


enum S2Val {
  S2VNull,
  S2VInt { value: integer },
  S2VText { value: text },
  S2VMap { entries: vector<S2Entry> },
}

struct S2Entry {
  key: S2Val,
  value: S2Val,
}

struct S2Dec {
  value: S2Val,
  next: integer,
  ok: boolean,
}

fn s2_read_v(bytes: vector<u8>, pos: integer, depth: integer) -> S2Dec {
  n = len(bytes);
  if pos + 1 >= n || depth > 8 { return S2Dec { value: S2VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
  tag = bytes[pos] ?? 0;
  arg = bytes[pos + 1] ?? 0;
  at = pos + 2;
  if tag == 1 { return S2Dec { value: S2VInt { value: arg - 100 }, next: at, ok: true }; }
  if tag == 2 {
    if at + arg > n { return S2Dec { value: S2VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    tb: vector<u8> = [];
    for k in 0..arg { tb += [bytes[at + k] ?? 0]; }
    return S2Dec { value: S2VText { value: text_from_bytes(tb) }, next: at + arg, ok: true };
  }
  if tag == 4 {
    entries: vector<S2Entry> = [];
    p = at;
    mok = true;
    for _ in 0..arg {
      if mok {
        kd = s2_read_v(bytes, p, depth + 1);
        if kd.ok {
          vd = s2_read_v(bytes, kd.next, depth + 1);
          if vd.ok {
            kv = kd.value;
            vv = vd.value;
            entries += [S2Entry { key: kv, value: vv }];
            p = vd.next;
          } else { mok = false; }
        } else { mok = false; }
      }
    }
    if !mok { return S2Dec { value: S2VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    return S2Dec { value: S2VMap { entries: entries }, next: p, ok: true };
  }
  return S2Dec { value: S2VNull, next: pos, ok: false };
}

fn s2_dec(bytes: vector<u8>) -> S2Dec { s2_read_v(bytes, 0, 0) }

fn text_of(v: S2Val) -> text {
  match v { S2VText { value } => { return "{value}"; }, _ => {} }
  return "-";
}

fn s2_get(m: S2Val, key: text) -> S2Val {
  match m {
    S2VMap { entries } => {
      for e in entries {
        match e.key { S2VText { value } => { if value == key { return e.value; } }, _ => {} }
      }
    },
    _ => {}
  }
  return S2VNull;
}

/// The decoded text formatted into another (a root: the frame is its parameter).
fn shout(frame: vector<u8>) -> text {
  d = s2_dec(frame);
  if !d.ok { return "bad"; }
  match d.value { S2VText { value } => { return "<{value}>"; }, _ => {} }
  return "?";
}

/// Bytes, characters and a character walk of the decoded text.
fn measure(frame: vector<u8>) -> text {
  d = s2_dec(frame);
  match d.value {
    S2VText { value } => {
      upper = 0;
      for c in value { if c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z' { upper += 1; } }
      return "{size(value)}/{len(value)}/{upper}";
    },
    _ => {}
  }
  return "?";
}

fn lookup(frame: vector<u8>, key: text) -> text {
  d = s2_dec(frame);
  if !d.ok { return "bad"; }
  text_of(s2_get(d.value, key))
}

// d1 — ASCII and multi-byte texts as map keys and values: {"k": "Zeta", "é": "Ωmega"}.
fn test_ascii_and_multi_byte_runs() {
  f: vector<u8> = [4, 2, 2, 1, 107, 2, 4, 90, 101, 116, 97, 2, 2, 195, 169, 2, 6, 206, 169, 109, 101, 103, 97];
  assert(lookup(f, "k") == "Zeta" && lookup(f, "é") == "Ωmega" && lookup(f, "x") == "-", "d1 {lookup(f, \"k\")} {lookup(f, \"é\")}");
}

// d2 — a run that is not UTF-8 decodes to "" (the copy's conversion), and one that is:
// [0x41, 0xFF, 0x42] → ""; "AbCé" → 5 bytes, 4 characters, 2 upper-case.
fn test_invalid_and_valid_runs() {
  bad: vector<u8> = [2, 3, 65, 255, 66];
  good: vector<u8> = [2, 5, 65, 98, 67, 195, 169];
  assert(shout(bad) == "<>" && measure(good) == "5/4/2" && measure(bad) == "0/0/0", "d2 {shout(bad)} {measure(good)}");
}

// d3 — an empty run, a run ending exactly at the frame's end, a run one byte past it:
// [2, 0] → "<>"; [2, 3, 120, 121, 122] → "<xyz>"; [2, 4, 120, 121, 122] → "bad".
fn test_empty_exact_and_overlong_runs() {
  assert(shout([2, 0]) == "<>" && shout([2, 3, 120, 121, 122]) == "<xyz>" && shout([2, 4, 120, 121, 122]) == "bad", "d3");
}


enum S3Val {
  S3VNull,
  S3VInt { value: integer },
  S3VText { value: text },
  S3VMap { entries: vector<S3Entry> },
}

struct S3Entry {
  key: S3Val,
  value: S3Val,
}

struct S3Dec {
  value: S3Val,
  next: integer,
  ok: boolean,
}

fn s3_read_v(bytes: vector<u8>, pos: integer, depth: integer) -> S3Dec {
  n = len(bytes);
  if pos + 1 >= n || depth > 8 { return S3Dec { value: S3VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
  tag = bytes[pos] ?? 0;
  arg = bytes[pos + 1] ?? 0;
  at = pos + 2;
  if tag == 1 { return S3Dec { value: S3VInt { value: arg - 100 }, next: at, ok: true }; }
  if tag == 2 {
    if at + arg > n { return S3Dec { value: S3VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    tb: vector<u8> = [];
    for k in 0..arg { tb += [bytes[at + k] ?? 0]; }
    return S3Dec { value: S3VText { value: text_from_bytes(tb) }, next: at + arg, ok: true };
  }
  if tag == 4 {
    entries: vector<S3Entry> = [];
    p = at;
    mok = true;
    for _ in 0..arg {
      if mok {
        kd = s3_read_v(bytes, p, depth + 1);
        if kd.ok {
          vd = s3_read_v(bytes, kd.next, depth + 1);
          if vd.ok {
            kv = kd.value;
            vv = vd.value;
            entries += [S3Entry { key: kv, value: vv }];
            p = vd.next;
          } else { mok = false; }
        } else { mok = false; }
      }
    }
    if !mok { return S3Dec { value: S3VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    return S3Dec { value: S3VMap { entries: entries }, next: p, ok: true };
  }
  return S3Dec { value: S3VNull, next: pos, ok: false };
}

fn s3_dec(bytes: vector<u8>) -> S3Dec { s3_read_v(bytes, 0, 0) }

fn s3_text_of(v: S3Val) -> text {
  match v { S3VText { value } => { return "{value}"; }, _ => {} }
  return "-";
}

fn s3_get(m: S3Val, key: text) -> S3Val {
  match m {
    S3VMap { entries } => {
      for e in entries {
        match e.key { S3VText { value } => { if value == key { return e.value; } }, _ => {} }
      }
    },
    _ => {}
  }
  return S3VNull;
}

/// e1 — admitted: the text copied into an owned slot inside the root.
fn held(frame: vector<u8>) -> text {
  d = s3_dec(frame);
  t = s3_text_of(d.value);
  "{t}!"
}

/// e2 — the decoded value RETURNED out of the frame's function: declines (3).
fn keep(frame: vector<u8>) -> S3Val {
  d = s3_dec(frame);
  return d.value;
}

/// e3 — a decoded entry appended to the CALLER's collection, which outlives the frame.
fn stash(frame: vector<u8>, into: vector<S3Val>) {
  d = s3_dec(frame);
  into += [d.value];
}

/// e4 — the frame written after the decode: (1) fails, the text is what the decode read.
fn scribble(frame: vector<u8>) -> text {
  d = s3_dec(frame);
  frame[2] = 122;
  frame[3] = 122;
  s3_text_of(d.value)
}

fn ping() -> vector<u8> { [2, 4, 112, 105, 110, 103] }

// e1 — "ping" → "ping!".
fn test_a_text_copied_into_an_owned_slot() {
  assert(held(ping()) == "ping!", "e1 {held(ping())}");
}

// e2 — returned, then the frame rewritten to "zzzz": the value keeps "ping".
fn test_a_value_returned_out_of_its_frame() {
  f = ping();
  v = keep(f);
  for i in 2..6 { f[i] = 122; }
  assert(s3_text_of(v) == "ping" && s3_text_of(keep(f)) == "zzzz", "e2 {s3_text_of(v)}");
}

// e3 — two frames stashed into one caller vector, the first frame then rewritten and the
// second dropped: the stash reads "ping" and "ok".
fn test_a_value_stored_into_a_callers_collection() {
  box: vector<S3Val> = [];
  f = ping();
  stash(f, box);
  for i in 2..6 { f[i] = 120; }
  stash([2, 2, 111, 107], box);
  assert(len(box) == 2 && s3_text_of(box[0]) == "ping" && s3_text_of(box[1]) == "ok", "e3 {s3_text_of(box[0])} {s3_text_of(box[1])}");
}

// e4 — the frame written after the decode: "ping" stays; the caller's frame now reads "zzng".
fn test_the_frame_written_after_the_decode() {
  f = ping();
  t = scribble(f);
  assert(t == "ping" && f[2] == 122 && f[4] == 110, "e4 {t}");
}

// e5 — a capture: a closure built over a decoded text reads it after the frame changed.
fn test_a_captured_text() {
  f = ping();
  d = s3_dec(f);
  s = s3_text_of(d.value);
  g = fn(x: text) -> text { "{s}-{x}" };
  for i in 2..6 { f[i] = 113; }
  assert(g("a") == "ping-a", "e5 {g(\"a\")}");
}


enum S4Val {
  S4VNull,
  S4VInt { value: integer },
  S4VText { value: text },
  S4VBytes { value: vector<u8> },
  S4VMap { entries: vector<S4Entry> },
}

struct S4Entry {
  key: S4Val,
  value: S4Val,
}

struct S4Dec {
  value: S4Val,
  next: integer,
  ok: boolean,
}

fn s4_read_v(bytes: vector<u8>, pos: integer, depth: integer) -> S4Dec {
  n = len(bytes);
  if pos + 1 >= n || depth > 8 { return S4Dec { value: S4VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
  tag = bytes[pos] ?? 0;
  arg = bytes[pos + 1] ?? 0;
  at = pos + 2;
  if tag == 1 { return S4Dec { value: S4VInt { value: arg - 100 }, next: at, ok: true }; }
  if tag == 3 {
    if at + arg > n { return S4Dec { value: S4VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    bs: vector<u8> = [];
    for k in 0..arg { bs += [bytes[at + k] ?? 0]; }
    return S4Dec { value: S4VBytes { value: bs }, next: at + arg, ok: true };
  }
  if tag == 2 {
    if at + arg > n { return S4Dec { value: S4VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    tb: vector<u8> = [];
    for k in 0..arg { tb += [bytes[at + k] ?? 0]; }
    return S4Dec { value: S4VText { value: text_from_bytes(tb) }, next: at + arg, ok: true };
  }
  if tag == 4 {
    entries: vector<S4Entry> = [];
    p = at;
    mok = true;
    for _ in 0..arg {
      if mok {
        kd = s4_read_v(bytes, p, depth + 1);
        if kd.ok {
          vd = s4_read_v(bytes, kd.next, depth + 1);
          if vd.ok {
            kv = kd.value;
            vv = vd.value;
            entries += [S4Entry { key: kv, value: vv }];
            p = vd.next;
          } else { mok = false; }
        } else { mok = false; }
      }
    }
    if !mok { return S4Dec { value: S4VNull, next: pos, ok: false }; }
    return S4Dec { value: S4VMap { entries: entries }, next: p, ok: true };
  }
  return S4Dec { value: S4VNull, next: pos, ok: false };
}

fn s4_dec(bytes: vector<u8>) -> S4Dec { s4_read_v(bytes, 0, 0) }

/// The entry of map `m` under text key `key`, or null.
fn s4_get(m: S4Val, key: text) -> S4Val {
  match m {
    S4VMap { entries } => {
      for e in entries {
        match e.key { S4VText { value } => { if value == key { return e.value; } }, _ => {} }
      }
    },
    _ => {}
  }
  return S4VNull;
}


/// map of 3: "op" -> text "apply", "raw" -> bytes "hi", "k" -> bytes "xyz"

struct Acc { n: integer, bytes: integer, hits: integer }

fn tally(a: Acc, v: S4Val) {
  match v {
    S4VText { value } => {
      a.n += 1;
      a.bytes += size(value);
      if value == "op" { a.hits += 1; }
    },
    _ => {}
  }
}

fn tally_all(frame: vector<u8>) -> text {
  d = s4_dec(frame);
  a = Acc { n: 0, bytes: 0, hits: 0 };
  match d.value {
    S4VMap { entries } => {
      for e in entries {
        tally(a, e.key);
        tally(a, e.value);
      }
    },
    _ => {}
  }
  "{a.n} {a.bytes} {a.hits}"
}

fn tally_loop(frame: vector<u8>, n: integer) -> text {
  d = s4_dec(frame);
  a = Acc { n: 0, bytes: 0, hits: 0 };
  for r in 0..n {
    match d.value {
      S4VMap { entries } => { for e in entries { tally(a, e.key); } },
      _ => {}
    }
    a.hits += a.n;
  }
  "{a.n} {a.bytes} {a.hits}"
}

fn test_a_callee_reads_every_decoded_text() {
  s = tally_all(frame3());
  assert(s == "4 11 1", "tally_all: {s}");
}

fn test_a_loop_reads_what_the_callee_wrote() {
  s = tally_loop(frame3(), 3);
  assert(s == "9 18 21", "tally_loop: {s}");
}

